🚀 Week 3 – Day 6 Polymorphism, Abstraction & Encapsulation in Java ☕

----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

🧠 Introduction

These are three major pillars of Object-Oriented Programming (OOP):

✔ Polymorphism
✔ Abstraction
✔ Encapsulation

👉 They help create flexible, secure, and maintainable software.

------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

🔁 1. Polymorphism

Polymorphism means **one name, many forms**.

The same method can behave differently depending on context.

-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

🔹 Types of Polymorphism

1️⃣ Compile-time Polymorphism (Method Overloading)
2️⃣ Runtime Polymorphism (Method Overriding)

---

📌 Method Overloading

```java id="p1"
class Calculator {
    int add(int a, int b) {
        return a + b;
    }

    int add(int a, int b, int c) {
        return a + b + c;
    }
}
```

---

📌 Method Overriding

```java id="p2"
class Animal {
    void sound() {
        System.out.println("Animal sound");
    }
}

class Dog extends Animal {
    @Override
    void sound() {
        System.out.println("Dog barks");
    }
}
```

------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

🎭 2. Abstraction

Abstraction means **hiding implementation details and showing only essential features**.

-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

🔹 Abstract Class Example

```java id="a1"
abstract class Shape {
    abstract void draw();
}

class Circle extends Shape {
    void draw() {
        System.out.println("Drawing Circle");
    }
}
```

---

🔹 Interface Example

```java id="a2"
interface Animal {
    void sound();
}
```

-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

🔒 3. Encapsulation

Encapsulation means **wrapping data and methods together and restricting direct access**.

-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

📌 Example

```java id="e1"
class Employee {
    private double salary;

    public void setSalary(double salary) {
        this.salary = salary;
    }

    public double getSalary() {
        return salary;
    }
}
```

---

🎯 Benefits of Encapsulation

✔ Data security
✔ Controlled access
✔ Better maintainability

---

📊 Comparison

| Concept       | Purpose                           |
| ------------- | --------------------------------- |
| Polymorphism  | Same method, different behavior   |
| Abstraction   | Hide implementation details       |
| Encapsulation | Protect data using access control |

-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

🧠 Real-World Examples

* ATM machine → Abstraction
* Different payment methods → Polymorphism
* Bank account with private balance → Encapsulation

---

⚠️ Common Mistakes

❌ Forgetting `@Override`
❌ Accessing private variables directly
❌ Not implementing abstract methods

-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

📚 Key Takeaways

✔ Polymorphism enables flexible behavior
✔ Abstraction hides complexity
✔ Encapsulation secures data
✔ These are core OOP principles

